  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1) \n\nCooler airmass will continue to settle across the area tonight on a \nlow level northeasterly flow. Patchy drizzle will occur in the cool\ndamp air mass.\n\nMid level short wave will drop southeast from the Upper MS Valley\nand deepen and close off over the Ohio Valley on Wednesday. This \nwill work to amplify an inverted surface trough along the western \nslopes of the Appalachians. These features will bring some showers to\nthe area Tuesday night into Wednesday with the greater threat for \nrain over the eastern counties. \n\nThe closed low will track off to the east coast thru the end of the\nweek resulting in an extended dry period for the area during the \nlatter part of the week into the weekend. Highs look to moderate \ncloser to normal early next week.",
